:: A1_start
<<set $act to 1>><<give "coins">>
<blockquote>Night in Florence. Rain hits the roofs like small stones. You smell wet bread and smoke. A baker pushes a warm loaf into your hands. "From the old man," he whispers. Then he runs.</blockquote>

You break the bread. Inside is a paper, folded tight.

The words are backwards.

[[Open the paper|A1_letter]]

:: A1_letter
You know this trick. Leonardo writes like this in all his notebooks.

<div class="mirror">THGINDIM TA POHSKROW YM OT EMOC</div>
<div class="mirror">ENO ON LLET</div>

One word is bigger than the others: ''THGINDIM''.

When must you go? Write the word the right way round.

<<textbox "_guess" "">>
<<link "Read it">><<mirror _guess "midnight" "A1_letter_ok" "A1_letter_wrong">><</link>>

:: A1_letter_wrong
<<spend 3>>
The letters swim in front of your eyes.

Start at the right side. Read each letter to the left.

[[Try again|A1_letter]]

:: A1_letter_ok
//Come to my workshop at midnight. Tell no one.//

You put the paper in your shirt.

Then you see him. A man in a red hat, under a dark arch.

He is not looking at the rain. He is looking at you.

[[Walk into the market|A1_chase]]

:: A1_chase
<<spend 2>>
The night market is loud and full. Fish, onions, wet dogs.

You look back. The red hat is still there. Ten steps behind you. Now eight.

[[Hide under the fish stall|A1_hide]]
[[Run through the crowd|A1_run]]

:: A1_hide
<<spend 1>>
You drop under the table. The smell of fish is terrible.

Boots stop next to your face. Red boots. Wet.

You do not breathe.

The boots walk away.

[[Climb out|A1_rook]]

:: A1_run
<<spend 4>>
You run. You push past a man with a goat.

A basket falls. Apples roll everywhere. A woman shouts at you.

You do not stop. When you look back, the red hat is gone.

[[Keep going|A1_rook]]

:: A1_rook
A boy sits on a wall, eating one of the apples. Thin, fast eyes, a big smile.

"I am Rook. You want the old man's workshop, yes? Secret road. Two coins."

The long road is safe, but it is far. And the rain is getting worse.

[[Pay Rook|A1_pay_rook]]
[[Take the long road|A1_long_road]]

:: A1_pay_rook
<<take "coins">><<heart -1>><<trust "rook" 1>>
You give him the coins. Leonardo's coins. They were not yours to spend.

Rook bites one, then grins. "This way. Stay close."

He takes you over roofs and through a church kitchen. In ten minutes you are there.

[[Knock on the door|A1_workshop]]

:: A1_long_road
<<spend 2>><<set $flags.long_road to true>>
"Your loss," says Rook. He is gone before you can answer.

You walk for an hour. The rain finds every hole in your coat.

Your boots are full of water. Your candle in your pocket is wet too.

[[Knock on the door|A1_workshop]]

:: A1_workshop
Leonardo's workshop. Wooden wings hang from the ceiling like sleeping bats.

Leonardo looks old tonight. Old and afraid.

"There is a book, Luca. It explains how the world works. Dreams, time, love. Men want to burn it. You must find it first."

He puts a small mirror in your hand.

"The book does not lie. But people do. Trust the mirror, not the face."

<<give "mirror">>

[[Ask where the book is|A1_workshop_2]]

:: A1_workshop_2
"The Church of the Silent Bells. On the hill. Go tonight."

"Why me?"

"Because they watch me. Nobody watches a student." He smiles. "And you read backwards better than I do."

[[Leave the workshop|A1_end]]

:: A1_end [autosave]
<<set $flags.fire_seen to true>>
You close the door behind you. The street is quiet. Too quiet.

Then you hear a scream.

You turn. Orange light fills the workshop windows.

The workshop is on fire.

[[Run to the church|A2_start]]
